>swap.  How do I get linloader and milo onto the sda1 partition so I can
>setup autobooting?  sda1 is set up as a dos type partition.

With the milo & linload.exe floppy installed enter the following 
  command (neatness counts a whole lot on this step, so be careful!)

	dd if=/dev/fd0 of=/dev/sda1 bs=10240

     Should look like this:

	[root@dcg /root]# dd if=/dev/fd0 of=/dev/sda1 bs=10240
	144+0 records in
	144+0 records out
	[root@dcg /root]# 

>BTW, this system seems a bit slow compared to my 60 mhz pentium running
>redhat 3.03.  Is it me or is it really a dog?

It runs about as fast as a P-70.  Best way to increase speed is recompile
the kernel from async to sysc and double you disk I/O.

