> model of riser card that is installed, the cable for the external SCSI port
> may not be installed, so if you want to be able to hang external drives onto
> the UDB, ensure that it's still connected and working.
> 
> > Would it be a SCSI-II Fast or Wide HD that I would need, I don't  know 
> > what the difference is between the two.
> 
> SCSI-II Fast, *not* Wide, as the builtin controller is not capable of Wide.

We have had this discussion at work (about what to put in the PCI slot).
As was pointed out just about everything is already included on the MB
but we came up with the following that are not:

Multi-Port serial card

100-base-T network card (10-base-T is relatively slow)

ISDN card (although you can do ISDN through the serial port)

Video Capture card (if software comes to support it)

Obviously, you could also use an external scsi drive and keep the
PCI slot if any of the above interest you.

